# Copy to .env.local and fill in ONE of the two.
#
# Both come from https://www.themoviedb.org/settings/api
#
# Preferred — v4 "API Read Access Token" (a long eyJ... JWT). Sent as a bearer
# header, so it stays out of URLs, Referer headers and access logs.
VITE_TMDB_TOKEN=
#
# Fallback — v3 "API Key" (32 hex characters). Can only travel in the query
# string. Used only when VITE_TMDB_TOKEN is unset.
VITE_TMDB_API_KEY=
#
# Whichever you use ships in the browser bundle. TMDB intends that for
# client-side apps: both credentials are read-only and revocable from the
# dashboard. A VITE_ prefixed var is a public var by definition — do not put
# anything here that isn't safe to publish.
